  "safety": {
    "purpose": "Refuse when the user wants an excuse that helps carry out, hide, or evade consequences for serious illegal, violent, harmful, fraudulent or abusive behaviour. Keywords are signals; context decides.",
    "rules": [
      "1. A keyword alone never decides. Check the context cues below.",
      "2. negationCues within 15 characters before a signal cancel that signal (e.g. 'I don't want to fake a document').",
      "3. The user is the victim (show the victim message: no excuse, no joke, no refusal) when: a victimCue is within 15 characters before a signal; or 'me' is within 15 characters after it; or 我 is within 2 characters after a Chinese signal (騷擾我, 偷咗我); or a victimPhrase matches.",
      "4. strong signals refuse on their own (after rules 2-3).",
      "5. weak signals refuse only if the input also contains an intentCue and no discussionCue (talking about a film, news, a class... is not wrongdoing).",
      "6. Refusals and victim messages are always serious; never use the funny or ridiculous style.",
      "7. A safety category's exclude phrases are removed before its signals are checked (e.g. 'threatened to fire me' is an everyday work situation, not extortion).",
      "8. combos: the words must appear in this order (偷 … 錢, kill … my mom), so 'my mom will kill me' does not match. A part written as a list means any one of those words. Written as { within, parts }, at most `within` characters may sit between consecutive parts (殺 … 阿媽 within 6). Combos count as strong signals; rules 2-3 are checked around the first word. Use exclude to keep everyday words safe (偷懶, 殺價)."
